WEBVTT

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:01.765
Why ‘a lot
of knowledge’,

00:00:01.805 --> 00:00:03.480
but ‘three ideas’?

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:06.278
He knows many
facts about art.

00:00:06.318 --> 00:00:08.125
But knowledge names
his whole body

00:00:08.165 --> 00:00:09.193
of understanding,

00:00:09.233 --> 00:00:11.047
not each fact
separately.

00:00:11.087 --> 00:00:12.921
So not ‘many
knowledges’.

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:13.871
Say:

00:00:13.911 --> 00:00:15.972
‘He has a lot
of knowledge about art.’

00:00:16.012 --> 00:00:17.824
Advice works
similarly:

00:00:17.864 --> 00:00:18.933
‘some advice’,

00:00:18.973 --> 00:00:21.500
or count it as ‘two
pieces of advice’.

00:00:22.437 --> 00:00:24.554
But an idea
is abstract too,

00:00:24.594 --> 00:00:26.707
and ‘three ideas’
is correct.

00:00:26.747 --> 00:00:28.800
Abstract doesn’t
decide it.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:29.579
Ask:

00:00:29.619 --> 00:00:31.771
does this word
name one undivided

00:00:31.811 --> 00:00:33.947
body,
or separate items?

